00:03:43.539 --> 00:03:45.539
Just a few things I want to update you on.

00:03:45.539 --> 00:03:48.539
We've got a lot that we're working on right now.

00:03:48.539 --> 00:03:51.539
Fortunately not everything we can talk about at this point in time,

00:03:51.539 --> 00:03:53.539
but there are some exciting things in the work.

00:03:53.539 --> 00:03:56.539
I know Tyler and Mayor Parker,

00:03:56.539 --> 00:03:58.539
who represent the city on our board.

00:03:58.539 --> 00:04:00.539
There are a lot of the things that we're doing on.

00:04:00.539 --> 00:04:02.539
Working on, but a couple of things before I do that,

00:04:02.539 --> 00:04:04.540
I just want to talk a little bit about why we did the

00:04:04.540 --> 00:04:06.540
proclamations tonight.

00:04:06.540 --> 00:04:08.540
So every year, the River Bottom Sportsman,

00:04:08.540 --> 00:04:11.540
along with the Mid-American Chapter of the Paralyzed Veterans of America,

00:04:11.540 --> 00:04:13.540
the host, what we call the Great Dear Hot.

00:04:13.540 --> 00:04:17.540
It's an annual outdoor recreational activity for disabled,

00:04:17.540 --> 00:04:20.540
paralyzed veterans, and local veteran.

00:04:20.540 --> 00:04:22.540
And so we're very excited about the hunters

00:04:22.540 --> 00:04:24.540
that we have participating this year,

00:04:24.540 --> 00:04:27.540
including our very own council member, Kyle Jones.

00:04:27.540 --> 00:04:29.540
We'll be participating this year.

00:04:29.540 --> 00:04:30.540
We're very excited about that.

00:04:30.540 --> 00:04:33.540
I gave each one of you a schedule of events,

00:04:33.540 --> 00:04:35.540
so that you know what's going on.

00:04:35.540 --> 00:04:38.540
We do want to remind you that all of the meals

00:04:38.540 --> 00:04:40.540
are open to the public.

00:04:40.540 --> 00:04:42.540
You're welcome to come and join us,

00:04:42.540 --> 00:04:43.540
especially on Friday.

00:04:43.540 --> 00:04:47.540
That's the big fish fry and everything else we do on that Friday.

00:04:47.540 --> 00:04:52.540
But the hunt this year runs October 29th through November 1st.

00:04:52.540 --> 00:04:54.540
The hunters arrive on the 29th.

00:04:54.540 --> 00:04:58.540
The opening ceremony is on the 9 a.m.

00:04:58.540 --> 00:05:01.540
A Commerce High School gymnasium on the 30th.

00:05:01.540 --> 00:05:07.240
And then the activities will run, like I said, through Saturday.

00:05:07.240 --> 00:05:09.240
And if we need it, we leave Sunday open.

00:05:09.240 --> 00:05:12.240
If we still have some veterans who are participating

00:05:12.240 --> 00:05:14.240
that happen to harvest it yet,

00:05:14.240 --> 00:05:16.240
we do have that one extra day to make that happen.

00:05:16.240 --> 00:05:18.240
But we feel pretty confident.

00:05:18.240 --> 00:05:21.240
We've got a good field general out there this year.

00:05:21.240 --> 00:05:23.240
Jody Francisco runs the field operations.

00:05:23.240 --> 00:05:26.240
We're excited about the spots that we have set up.

00:05:26.240 --> 00:05:29.240
We anticipate everyone harvesting early.

00:05:29.240 --> 00:05:31.240
We actually added an extra hunt this year.

00:05:31.240 --> 00:05:35.240
So normally every veteran used to make four hunts.

00:05:35.240 --> 00:05:39.240
They do a morning and afternoon on Friday and Saturday.

00:05:39.240 --> 00:05:42.240
We actually added an extra one on Thursday afternoon.

00:05:42.240 --> 00:05:45.240
So you have five opportunities this year and a set of four.

00:05:45.240 --> 00:05:47.240
So we're pretty excited about that.

00:05:47.240 --> 00:05:50.240
We're also pretty excited that Thursday night.

00:05:50.240 --> 00:05:54.500
All of this by the way takes place at Jack's house on the dial room.

00:05:54.500 --> 00:05:56.500
We'll form in the barn.

00:05:56.500 --> 00:05:59.500
Thursday night October 30th.

00:05:59.500 --> 00:06:00.500
We're going to be ready.
